WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.901
[music playing]

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.168
 Kyle and Ben, congratulations.

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:05.304
You guys are moving
forward into round three.

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:07.707
Only the man next to you
stands between you, the title

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.542
of "Forged in Fire" Champion,
and that coveted check

00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:11.578
for $10,000.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.179
In round three we're
going to send you guys

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.582
back home to recreate an
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.450
That weapon is--

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:20.686
[music playing]

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:21.654
--the Vajra-musti.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.522
 Wow.

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:24.156
DOUG MARCAIDA:
Originating in India,

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:26.959
the Vajra-musti is an
edged knuckle duster.

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.961
The unique design
features sharpened blades

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.730
on every side of
the handle, making

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.332
it a specialty
weapon only wielded

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.400
by well-trained Indian warriors.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.036
The sharp edges on all
sides provided the user

00:00:37.102 --> 00:00:38.772
with a wide range
of lethal attacks,

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:42.608
from deadly stabs and slashes
to devastating punches.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.711
A traditional Indian
martial art where the weapon

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.513
is tied to the fist of wrestlers
has lineage dating back

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.216
to the Middle Ages and
is still practiced today

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.251
by professional
wrestlers in India, using

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.987
non-lethal knuckle dusters.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.121
 I don't even--

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.024 line:0%
[laughs] I don't even
know what to say.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.325
The closest thing
I've seen to that

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:01.093
is probably a pair
of brass knuckles.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.396
 We're going to send you
guys home for four days.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.165
And when you guys come back,
I want to see two blades

00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:08.534
worth at least $10,000 apiece.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.370
So do your absolute best
work, and good luck.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:12.772
We'll see you in four days.
- Awesome.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:13.539
Good luck, man.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.474 line:7%
 Good luck.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:18.845 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:23.049
KYLE: I feel good to
be back home, here

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.283
in Bellows Falls, Vermont.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.754
And we're going to
make the Vajra-musti.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.790
I've never made a Vajra-musti,
or anything close to it.

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:34.927
So I decided to use 1084 carbon
steel because it's something

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.096
I'm more familiar with.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.632
I think the most difficult
part of the challenge

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.033
will be making the handle--

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.669
something that I'm
definitely going to have

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.036
to pay a lot of attention to.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:47.173
[music playing]

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.309
The two smaller blades
are basically the same.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.710
One's a little longer
than the other.

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:55.514
You know, then the other
blade is just a big rectangle.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:59.852
Five hours into it,
I feel pretty good.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.153
One more soak in the forge.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.856
And then I'll quench them.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.827
I got all the forging out of
the way, so I'm feeling good.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:13.031
End of day one, and I'm really
glad I got the heat treat done.

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:14.633
Looks good.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.169 line:7%
[barking]

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:20.673
BEN: Day two, I'm a
little tired this morning.

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:24.244
But I feel great, ready to
get this show on the road.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.479
I decide that I'm going to go
with a torch heat treatment,

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:29.615
because the handle
doesn't need to be hard.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:33.152
I just need the blades hard
and the knuckle blade hard.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:33.953
[sizzles]

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.188
So I did one.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.156
And I'm scared I'm going
to crack it in half.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.759
Because right after the
quench, it is brittle.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:46.999
So any little shock or hit could
cause catastrophic cracking.

00:02:47.065 --> 00:02:49.736
Luckily, I don't see any cracks.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.837
So I think the quench went well.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.839 line:7%
That's going to have to do.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.408 line:7%
[music playing]

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.410 line:0%
KYLE: It's beginning
of day two, and I

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:58.644 line:7%
can't wait to get started.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.346
For the handle, I'm
going to go with copper.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:03.749
It's moving a lot better than
I thought it was going to.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.853
I want to pay really
close attention to detail.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.587
I want to make a $10,000 knife.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.423
Today I'm able to
remove three pounds

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:13.092
off a five-pound chunk
of copper and knock

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.627
out a nice workable piece.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.129
Tomorrow I'd like to get
the handle all finished up

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.698
and the blades fitted on.

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.566
Well, that's basically it.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.234 line:7%
[music playing]

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:23.402 line:7%
BEN: It's day four.

00:03:23.468 --> 00:03:25.938
Ready to get this thing done.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:31.210
So I just got done doing the
profiling on my Vajra-musti.

00:03:31.276 --> 00:03:32.445
Feels pretty good.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.280
I'm going to start doing
fit up on the handle.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.950
[music playing]

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.284
I'm feeling great.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.588
At the end of the day, I
used every minute that I had.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.256
There's definitely some
finishing touches that I didn't

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.292
get to that I wish I had.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.094
Mainly, the handle.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.695
I'm hoping that
there's not, you know,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:53.032
major hot spots around the
knuckles or anything like that.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.833
It can look like crap.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.437
But as long as it feels
comfortable in your hand,

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.639
you know, that's fine.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.639
I feel good.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.442
I mean, I definitely did
the best that I could.

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.346
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.115
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:12.151
I will take your weapon and
deliver multiple lethal blows

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.053
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.488
Kyle, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.256
 Oh yeah.

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:19.892
[rock music playing]

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:23.496
[squishing]

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.733
[thuds]

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.502
[squishes]

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:35.641
 Wow.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:36.742
 [exhales]

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.978
 All right, Kyle, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.312
I was worried about
the finger wells

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.448
that you had there, that
they would be an issue,

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:44.083
especially when I'm punching.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.417
No issues there.

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:48.220
I like the fact that
as it gets slippery,

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.155
it gave me a very good grip.

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:52.191
Overall, it is a
beautiful piece.

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.793
And your weapon will kill.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:55.561
 Oh yeah.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:56.829
 All right, Ben.
Your turn, sir.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:57.563
Are you ready?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.364
 I'm ready.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.699
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:02.668
[music playing]

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.704
[squishes]

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:09.007
[squishing]

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.976
[grunts]

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:12.979
[thuds]

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.220
 All right, Ben, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.523
The edges are very sharp.

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:27.026
But there are some sharp
edges that you have in here.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:30.129
Every movement started to
give me a little bruise

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.897
and cut off some
skin right there.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:37.370
But in terms of what this
weapon will do, it will kill.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:38.337
BEN: Thanks, Doug.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.673
 My hand.

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:44.576
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the strength test.

00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:46.078
To test the strength
and durability

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:49.281
of your Vajra-mustis, as well
as their overall construction,

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:51.250
I'll be stabbing and
punching into this sheet

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:52.317
metal and chain.

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:53.152
Kyle, you're up first.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:53.886
You ready for this?

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:54.787
 Yeah.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:58.424
[music playing]

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.761
[blade impacts]

00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:11.003
[clanking]

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:16.709
 All right, Kyle.

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:19.545
In this strength test, your
two long blades held up great.

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:22.314
The center blade here took
some chipping on that chain.

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:23.582
I'm looking at the
grain in there.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.017
And it's-- it's pretty big.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.353
I would have liked to
have seen that refined.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.388
But in general, these
two blades held up well.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:30.155
Nice job.

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:30.923
 Awesome.

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:31.724
Thanks, Ben.

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.058
 All right, Ben, you're up.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:33.892
You ready for this?

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:35.361
 Sure am.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:36.962
[music playing]

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:40.633
[blade impacts]

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.611
[clanking]

00:06:53.011 --> 00:06:56.949
[music playing]

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.083
 All right, Ben.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.520
Well, the first thing I feel
when I pick this weapon up

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:01.621
is its sheer mass.

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:03.422
I mean, it's a
heavy, heavy weapon.

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.024
That did you some justice
in the strength test.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.093
The only thing I could
see is a little bit

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:08.560
of glinting on the lower blade.

00:07:08.627 --> 00:07:12.831
But the middle blade, it took
a pretty major deflection

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:13.966
right here.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.334
It kind of cracked.

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:17.103
One more little--
little hit here

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:18.437
and that would just come off.

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.039
The main thing working
against you on this blade

00:07:21.106 --> 00:07:23.642
is the rough inner surface.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:26.145
I couldn't really find a real
comfortable way of getting

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:28.047
this finger out of harm's way.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.949
But after the strength
test, it's all in one piece.

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:31.717
Nice job.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:34.052
 Thank you.

00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:37.322
 All right, bladesmiths, we
know your weapons can kill.

00:07:37.389 --> 00:07:38.791
And we know they are strong.

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:40.726
Now it's time to find out
just how sharp they are.

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:42.261
To find out, I'll
take your weapons

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:46.666
and deliver some stabs and
slices on these spice bags.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.133
Kyle, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.101
 Yup.

00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:50.870
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:54.474
[music playing]

00:07:58.877 --> 00:08:02.148
[blade impacts]

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:12.859
All right, Kyle, let's
talk about your weapon.

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:13.826
It is comfortable.

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:15.527
It's a good fit on my hand.

00:08:15.594 --> 00:08:17.329
It's got a pointy
enough tip over there.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:20.298
But with that one piece where
you're missing some edges,

00:08:20.365 --> 00:08:21.867
it was more of a jagged cut.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:25.203
When it came to stabbing
and slashing on both weapons

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.973
on each end, it'll cut.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:28.608
Good job.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.176
 Thank you, Doug.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:31.210
 Ben, your turn, sir.

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:32.044
You ready?

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:33.045
 Ready, let's go.

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:34.013
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do it.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.983
[music playing]

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:43.523
[blade impacts]

00:08:52.564 --> 00:08:54.933
All right, Ben, let's
talk about your weapon.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.603
The weight that you have
here back up the cut,

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.337
because you have
very sharp edges.

00:08:59.404 --> 00:09:00.806
And the cuts are very deep.

00:09:00.872 --> 00:09:02.742
But my hand, when
I'm making impact,

00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:05.511
still rubs on the
inside of your handle.

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:08.981
But other than that sir,
your beast, it will cut.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.616
 Thanks, Doug.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.518
[music playing]

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:13.986
GRADY POWELL: All right, guys.

00:09:14.052 --> 00:09:17.222
You guys both came through with
unbelievable pieces of work,

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.324
verging on art.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.493
And they performed almost
equally on all the tests.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.495
Unfortunately, we can
only send one of you guys

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:23.862
home with the title
of "Forged in Fire"

00:09:23.929 --> 00:09:26.765
champion and a
check for $10,000.

00:09:26.798 --> 00:09:28.367
And our champion today is--

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:30.836
[suspenseful music]

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:31.370
--Kyle.

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:32.538
Congratulations.

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:34.072
Ben, unfortunately,
you're not walking

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:34.874
home the champion today.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.141
Doug's going to tell you why.

00:09:36.175 --> 00:09:37.676
DOUG MARCAIDA: Ben, I
commend you on building

00:09:37.743 --> 00:09:39.010
a very unique weapon.

00:09:39.077 --> 00:09:42.515
But only your handle
affected both of us

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:43.749
when we were testing it.

00:09:43.815 --> 00:09:45.985
And for that reason,
we're sending you home.

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:47.485
 Totally understand.

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:48.754
 Well, Ben, you
obviously showed

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.089
you have what it takes
to be in the forge

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:51.557
and to compete with
some of the best.

00:09:51.623 --> 00:09:53.058
But unfortunately,
the time has come.

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:55.260
I'm going to have to ask you
to leave the Forged floor.

00:09:55.293 --> 00:09:56.661
 Thank you, guys.

00:09:56.728 --> 00:09:57.963
This was awesome, for sure.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:58.630
 Good job.

00:09:58.697 --> 00:09:59.765
 Kyle, amazing job.

00:09:59.832 --> 00:10:00.932
Honestly, I feel great.

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:03.235
I mean, it was an
amazing experience.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:04.603
I'm super happy for Kyle.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.905
I had a feeling that
handle was going to get me.

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:09.174
But I busted my
butt and honestly

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.542
did the best that I could.

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:13.546
So I don't have any regrets.

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:15.414
GRADY POWELL: Well,
Kyle, congratulations.

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:18.717
You'll be leaving here with the
title "Forged in Fire" Champion

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:20.252
and a check for $10,000.

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:21.020
Congratulations.

00:10:21.053 --> 00:10:22.288
 Thank you.

00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:23.822
My wife's going
to be super pumped

00:10:23.855 --> 00:10:27.025
when I tell her that I'm the
next "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:27.092 --> 00:10:29.094
 What are you going to
do with that cash, man?

00:10:29.127 --> 00:10:30.696
 My wife and I are
probably going to use it

00:10:30.762 --> 00:10:31.864
for a down payment on a house.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.398
- That's absolutely fantastic.
- Nice.

00:10:33.465 --> 00:10:34.667
 Cool.

00:10:34.734 --> 00:10:37.169
 18 months ago, I would have
never imagined being here

00:10:37.236 --> 00:10:37.936
today.

00:10:38.003 --> 00:10:38.704
Hell yeah.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:39.871
I'm a "Forged in Fire" Champion.

00:10:39.938 --> 00:10:40.406
[laughs]

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:41.473
[music playing]

